      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "What To Expect",
        "intro": "Some dogs settle within the first few minutes: a lowered tail, slower breathing, lying down instead of pacing. Others need two or three wears before they stop noticing the vest is even there and start associating it with the calm that follows. A small number of dogs don't respond much at all — that's a real, honest possibility, and not every dog reacts to gentle pressure the same way.",
        "note": "If your dog seems more distressed in the vest — not less — take it off and talk to your vet before trying again.",
        "closing": "Every dog settles differently — but they don't have to do it alone.",
        "show_atc": true
      }
